1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,247
In this town, everyone has a skip button.

2
00:00:02,327 --> 00:00:03,951
It's right here, on your wrist.

3
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:06,046
Press it, and time jumps forward.

4
00:00:06,193 --> 00:00:07,747
People use it to skip school.

5
00:00:07,827 --> 00:00:09,347
Boring conversations.

6
00:00:09,427 --> 00:00:10,547
Traffic jams.

7
00:00:10,627 --> 00:00:11,747
Even heartbreak.

8
00:00:11,827 --> 00:00:13,913
Your mom skips her whole drive to work.

9
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:16,147
Your teacher skips grading forty tests.

10
00:00:16,227 --> 00:00:18,313
Everyone is always somewhere else.

11
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:19,447
Except you.

12
00:00:19,527 --> 00:00:21,713
You're the only one whose button doesn't work.

13
00:00:21,793 --> 00:00:23,680
You've pressed it a thousand times.

14
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:24,630
Nothing.

15
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:26,647
You even took it to the repair shop.

16
00:00:26,727 --> 00:00:29,647
The man just laughed. "That's never happened before."

17
00:00:29,727 --> 00:00:31,847
So you live through every boring minute.

18
00:00:31,927 --> 00:00:33,180
Every math class.

19
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:34,780
Every long car ride.

20
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:36,580
Every awkward silence.

21
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:38,547
Kids at school call you Slow-Mo.

22
00:00:38,627 --> 00:00:40,813
Your best friend Jayden thinks it's hilarious.

23
00:00:40,893 --> 00:00:42,013
He skips everything.

24
00:00:42,093 --> 00:00:44,245
Tests. Chores. Sundays.

25
00:00:44,393 --> 00:00:46,980
He even skipped his own birthday party. Twice.

26
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:49,180
"Why would anyone live the boring parts?"

27
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:51,247
One Monday, he holds his button down.

28
00:00:51,327 --> 00:00:52,513
And doesn't let go.

29
00:00:52,593 --> 00:00:54,047
He skips an entire week.

30
00:00:54,127 --> 00:00:56,867
Seven whole days. Gone in one blink.

31
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:58,813
His seat in class stays empty.

32
00:00:58,893 --> 00:01:02,847
Monday. Tuesday. Wednesday. Thursday. Friday.

33
00:01:02,927 --> 00:01:04,913
On Saturday, someone knocks on your door.

34
00:01:04,993 --> 00:01:05,923
It's Jayden.

35
00:01:06,093 --> 00:01:07,113
But he looks older.

36
00:01:07,193 --> 00:01:08,380
His hair is longer.

37
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:09,680
His hands are shaking.

38
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:10,847
He's terrified.

39
00:01:10,927 --> 00:01:12,147
He grabs your wrist.

40
00:01:12,227 --> 00:01:13,380
"Don't fix your button."

41
00:01:13,460 --> 00:01:15,347
"We're still awake during the parts we skip."

42
00:01:15,427 --> 00:01:18,380
"Our bodies keep going. We're stuck inside, watching."

43
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:21,513
"I felt every second of that week. And I couldn't move."

44
00:01:21,593 --> 00:01:23,047
"And we're not alone in there."

45
00:01:23,127 --> 00:01:24,613
"Something else is driving."

46
00:01:24,693 --> 00:01:25,947
Then his button blinks.

47
00:01:26,027 --> 00:01:27,247
His face goes blank.

48
00:01:27,327 --> 00:01:29,313
And he walks away. Smiling.

49
00:01:29,393 --> 00:01:30,547
You look down the street.

50
00:01:30,627 --> 00:01:32,180
Your neighbor's button is glowing.

51
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:33,480
So is the mailman's.

52
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:34,647
So is your mom's.

53
00:01:34,727 --> 00:01:37,447
The whole street is skipping. All at the same time.

54
00:01:37,527 --> 00:01:38,747
Their eyes are empty.

55
00:01:38,827 --> 00:01:40,113
But they're all smiling.

56
00:01:40,193 --> 00:01:41,547
That night, you can't sleep.

57
00:01:41,627 --> 00:01:43,147
You stare at your broken button.

58
00:01:43,227 --> 00:01:44,647
And for the first time ever...

59
00:01:44,727 --> 00:01:45,747
it lights up.

60
00:01:45,827 --> 00:01:46,847
You didn't touch it.

61
00:01:46,927 --> 00:01:48,380
Your hands are under the blanket.

62
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:49,760
Someone else presses it.

